            <ArticleTitle>[Burgdorf's reaction (painful acral erythema) in patients with acute lymphoblastic leukemia following medium-dose methotrexate therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>462-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Erythematous changes of the palms with associated oedema, blistering and desquamation were observed in two children during chemotherapy for acute lymphoblastic leukaemia, after methotrexate in doses of 1,000 mg/m2. These changes correspondent to those described in the literature as Burgdorf's reaction. In Poland it was never reported as yet.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
